<title>GERMANY: Commerzbank seeks higher BRE stake.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank seeks higher BRE stake.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Commerzbank AG said on Friday it would be seeking to raise its stake in Poland's Bank Rozwoju Exportu (BRE) through acquisitions of existing shares rather than newly-created ones.</p>
<p>&quot;It will be from existing shareholders rather than through a new capital issue,&quot; Commerzbank spokesman Peter Pietsch said in response to enquiries.</p>
<p>He declined to give further details.</p>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission (KPW) said on Thursday it had approved an acquisition of 11.9 percent of BRE by Commerzbank, a deal which would take the German bank's stake up to 32.9 percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
